WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:03.755
The machine keeping a patient breathing can

00:00:03.755 --> 00:00:06.960
also expose delicate airway cells to damaging forces.

00:00:10.925 --> 00:00:15.180
We modelled one mechanical event in cultured rat alveolar

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:19.434
epithelial cells: a single air bubble passing over a monolayer.

00:00:24.342 --> 00:00:28.481
We used a parallel-plate chamber, fluorescence live-dead staining,

00:00:28.481 --> 00:00:32.620
and microscopy to examine what happened after bubble propagation.

00:00:37.425 --> 00:00:42.324
Our experiment tested whether pretreatment with dexamethasone or

00:00:42.324 --> 00:00:47.223
trans-dehydroandrosterone could change the cells' susceptibility before exposure.

00:00:52.675 --> 00:00:58.002
Under these in-vitro conditions, bubble flow injured cells. Pretreatment significantly

00:00:58.002 --> 00:01:03.329
reduced the measured cell death, alongside changes in cellular mechanics.

00:01:09.217 --> 00:01:14.132
A culture chamber is not a ventilated patient. The result is a

00:01:14.132 --> 00:01:19.047
mechanistic finding and a question for further translation, not a clinical prescription.
